-- title:
--   Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformising family on the fine moduli scheme
-- statement:
--   The statement is an existence assertion about a $\tilde\Gamma$-equivariant family of nilpotent points of the fine moduli scheme of fake elliptic curves with full level structure; it is stated relative to a long list of data, which are grouped below.
--
--   **Arithmetic base data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$ and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$ (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Coefficient rings.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi\in\mathcal O$ is irreducible, $\mathcal O$ is complete for the ideal $(\pi)$ (`hcomplete`), $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $r$ and $\pi$ generate the same ideal (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero field which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $Onr$ is a characteristic-zero domain and $\mathcal O$-algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_complete`, `hOnr_max`); every element of $Onr$ satisfies, modulo $\pi$, a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $Onr$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}$ modulo $\pi$ (`hFr`). Finally `vdet` is a homomorphism from $GL_2(K_0)$ to $\mathbb Z$ written multiplicatively, characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$; thus it is the $\pi$-valuation of the determinant. For $\psi:Onr\to B$ write $\psi^{\flat}=\psi\circ Fr^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ for the Frobenius twist occurring below.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and the completion at a finite place $v$ is a division algebra precisely when $v$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$), and a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point map `pt` assigning to each ring $S$, each morphism $s$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and each fake elliptic curve of level $N$ over $S$ (an abelian scheme of relative fibre dimension two with commutative relative group law, a $\Lambda$-action satisfying a trace condition, and a level-$N$ subscheme) a point over $s$, such that `pt` is a coarse moduli structure (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullbacks, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An integer $n\geq 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`), a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` on full level-$n$ structures which is a fine moduli structure (`hM`), a group $G$ with $\rho:G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and $\chi:G\to\Lambda$ forming a level twist action (`hρ`: $\rho$ acts over the base, twisting a level structure by $\chi(g)$ moves the point by $\rho(g)$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, surjective and injective modulo $n$). A morphism $p:M\to\mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`), and compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for extra level-$\ell$ structures (`h𝒴`) with degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) realising, respectively, forgetting the extra level (`hd₀`) and passing to the $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`). Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`), an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that the intersection order $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$ (`hv`). The group $\tilde\Gamma$ is the subgroup of units integral away from $v$ with respect to $R_1$ (`hΓt`). Elements $s_\ell$ and ideles $sf_\ell$ for $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ with `hs` (four clauses): $sf_\ell$ agrees with $s_\ell$ at all places not containing $r$, is trivial at the places containing $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in the level Hecke set of $\mathrm{meetOrder}\,R_1\,n_1$ relative to $\Lambda_1$ when $\ell\mid N$ and in its prime Hecke set otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$; and $\tilde\Gamma_\ell$ is defined as the intersection of $\tilde\Gamma$ with its conjugate by $s_\ell$ (`hΓtℓ`). A unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Data on the special fibre.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that $\Lambda$ contains all rational integers; a coordinatisation $\mathrm{coord}:\Lambda\to W(\mathbb F_{r^{2}})^{2}$ satisfying `hcoord` (additive, unital, multiplicative in the twisted sense, injective, with dense image and compatible with reduced traces). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $Onr/(\pi)$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of dimension two over the same ring, of height four (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ for $A_0$ in two variables, with `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Endomorphism families $e,e':\tilde\Gamma\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`, subject to: `hE1` ($(e_\gamma,e'_\gamma)$ an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure), `hE1mul` ($e_{\gamma\gamma'}$ followed by multiplication by $r^{i}$ equals $e_{\gamma'}$ followed by $e_\gamma$ followed by multiplication by $r^{j}$, for some $i,j$), `hE1sc` (rational integral scalars act as such up to $r$-powers), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e_\gamma$ is a scalar up to an $r$-power then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism of the centraliser of the $W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$-action and of $\varpi$ in $\operatorname{End}(X_0)$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$), `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ carries a labelling $\tilde\Gamma\to\Lambda$ intertwining $e_\gamma$ with the $\Lambda$-action, multiplicative modulo $n$ and compatible with scalars modulo $n$), `hE4` (over algebraically closed fields, every $r$-power isogeny pair preserving the level on a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes from some $e_\gamma$ up to $r$-powers). An order $R_2\leq R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) containing $r$-power multiples of all of $R_1$ (`hR₂r`), with endomorphisms $\hat e$ of $A_0$ over the base (`hê`) satisfying `hE5a` (additivity on points, commutation with $\Lambda$, preservation of the level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unitality, $\hat e_{xy}=\hat e_y$ followed by $\hat e_x$, and agreement with integral multiplication), `hE5c` ($\hat e_{\bar x}$ followed by $\hat e_x$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$), `hE5d` (compatibility of $\hat e$ with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\tilde\Gamma$) and `hE5e` (a single $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ realising both the $\tilde\Gamma$-clause of `hE2` and its analogue for $R_2$).
--
--   **Deformation-theoretic side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota:W(\mathbb F_{r^{2}})\to Onr$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $Onr/(r)$ which is special for the structure map induced by $\iota$ (`hΦ`) and of height four (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $MD$ over $Onr$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a map $\eta$ sending rigidified objects over $r$-nilpotent rings to points of $MD$, with `hη` (three clauses: on Noetherian rings $\eta$ identifies admissible rigidified objects exactly up to isomorphism, commutes with base change, and is Zariski-locally surjective). A ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $W(\mathbb F_{r^2})$-action and of $\varpi$ on $\operatorname{End}(\Phi)$ into $M_2(K_0)$ with `hE₀`: $E_0$ is injective and its image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$, in the precise sense that for some $m$ every matrix over $\mathcal O$ multiplied by $r^{m}$ lies in the image, and $r^{m}$ times every value of $E_0$ is integral. A comparison $eD$ from the functor of points of $MD$ with a lift of $Onr$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $Onr$ with the functor $\Omega$ of Deligne data over $(K_0,\pi)$ — the formal upper half-plane — on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, satisfying `hnatD` (naturality), `hbijD` (bijectivity), `hfstD` (the first component is the given algebra map), `hGLD` (the $GL_2(K_0)$-action on moduli points corresponds to the twisted action on pairs), `hPiD` (a $\pi$-translate corresponds to twisting the first component by $Fr$ and leaving the Deligne datum unchanged) and `hPiexD` (existence of $\pi$-translates). A ring map $\kappa:Onr/(\pi)\to Onr/(r)$ compatible with the reductions (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ which is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner datum at $\bar r$ on $A_0$.** A curve $A_{0w}$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w'$ realising the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair $b_w,b_w'$ between $A_{0w}$ and $A_0$ with $b_w$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, which asserts that a single $g\in GL_2(K_0)$ realises simultaneously the $\tilde\Gamma$-clause of `hE2` and an element $\varepsilon_w$ of the centraliser inducing $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ on formal coordinates with image $r^{k_w'}g\iota_0(\bar w)g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison $\Xi$ and the element $g_0$.** A map $\Xi$ sending, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\psi:Onr\to B$, a rigidified fake elliptic curve over $(B,\psi)$ to a point of the moduli functor, subject to `hΞleg` (over connected $B$ the algebra component of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (compatibility with pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves admitting the displayed comparison data on the reductions and the $r$-power commutation) and `hΞdef` (over connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, for a curve carrying formal module data via $\mathrm{coord}$ there are $j\leq 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with the given formal module, transporting the rigidification, such that $\Xi$ is the point built from $\psi\circ Fr^{-j}$ and $\eta(t)$). An element $g_0\in GL_2(K_0)$ with `heqΓ` (translating a rigidification by $e_\gamma$ corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ on $\Xi$, for some $c\in\mathbb Z$) and `heqW` (the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, over connected $B$ in which $\bar r$ is invertible and with the displayed comparison data, corresponds to the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$). Finally, the hypothesis `h2` that $2$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exist a group homomorphism $\tilde\theta:\tilde\Gamma\to G$ and a family $\Theta_f$ assigning to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent a map from $\bigl((Onr\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega(B)\bigr)\times G$ to the set of morphisms $\operatorname{Spec}B\to M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, such that all of the following hold. Throughout, say that a pair $(E,\varrho)$ consisting of a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $\psi^{\flat}$ *represents* $(\psi,P)$ if the algebra component of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is $\psi^{\flat}$ and the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action carries $eD(\Xi(E,\varrho))$ to $(\psi,P)$.
--
--   1.
--
--   (Naturality) $\Theta_f$ commutes with the functorial maps along every $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism between Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent.
--
--   2.
--
--   (Equivariance for $G$) For all $g,h\in G$ and all $x$ in the first two factors, applying the automorphism $\rho(h)$ to $\Theta_f(x,gh)$ gives $\Theta_f(x,g)$.
--
--   3.
--
--   (Equivariance for $\tilde\Gamma$) For $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ and $x,x'$ such that the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ carries $x$ to $x'$, one has $\Theta_f(x',\tilde\theta(\gamma)g)=\Theta_f(x,g)$ for all $g\in G$.
--
--   4.
--
--   (Infinitesimal lifting) For Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$, $B_0$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and a surjective $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $B\to B_0$ whose kernel has zero multiplication (any two elements killed by it have product zero), and for every $x_0$ over $B_0$ and every $B$-point $y$ of $M$ over the base whose image is $\Theta_f(x_0)$, there is a unique $x$ over $B$ lying over $x_0$ with $\Theta_f(x)=y$.
--
--   5.
--
--   (Geometric fibres) For an algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, and for $\psi,\psi':Onr\to k$, Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$ and $g,g'\in G$: $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g)=\Theta_f((\psi',P'),g')$ if and only if there is $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $g'=\tilde\theta(\gamma)g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and with $\psi'(y)=\psi\bigl(Fr^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}y\bigr)$ for every $y\in Onr$ which is fixed by $Fr^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all rational scalars $z\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $\tilde\theta(z)=1$.
--
--   6.
--
--   (Existence of the level transport) For Noetherian connected $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\psi$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ with a rigidification relative to $\psi^{\flat}$, and every formal module datum $(X,\theta)$ for $E$ via $\mathrm{coord}$, there is a full level-$n$ structure on $E$ which is a norm level transport of $P_0$ along the rigidification.
--
--   7.
--
--   (Uniqueness of the level transport) Any two full level-$n$ structures on $E$ which are norm level transports of $P_0$ along the same rigidification have the same underlying point.
--
--   8.
--
--   For Noetherian connected $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\psi$ and every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, there exist $E$ and a rigidification $\varrho$ relative to $\psi^{\flat}$ such that $(E,\varrho)$ represents $(\psi,P)$.
--
--   9.
--
--   Any two pairs $(E,\varrho)$, $(E',\varrho')$ representing the same $(\psi,P)$ over such a $B$ are related by an isomorphism $E\cong E'$ compatible with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level structure, together with comparison morphisms on the reductions and on the pulled-back copies of $A_0$ making the rigidification diagrams commute after multiplication by suitable powers of $r$.
--
--   10.
--
--   (Base change) For an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from $B$ to $B'$, both Noetherian, connected and with $\pi$ nilpotent, and for $(E,\varrho)$ representing $(\psi,P)$ over $B$, there exist $E'$ over $B'$ with a pullback morphism to $E$, and a rigidification $\varrho'$ relative to the corresponding twist, which is a pullback of $\varrho$, such that $(E',\varrho')$ represents the image of $(\psi,P)$ over $B'$.
--
--   11.
--
--   If $(E,\varrho)$ represents $(\psi,P)$ and $P_n$ is a norm level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$, then the morphism underlying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ is the one attached by `ptF` to the pair $(E,P_n)$ over the structure morphism of $B$.
--
--   12.
--
--   Under the same hypotheses, the morphism underlying $\Theta_f((\psi,P),1)$ followed by $p$ is the coarse moduli point attached by `pt` to $E$.
--
--   13.
--
--   ($\tilde\Gamma$-translation on the curve side) For Noetherian connected $B$, $(E,\varrho)$ representing $(\psi,P)$, $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ and $(\psi',P')$ the image of $(\psi,P)$ under the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$, there is a rigidification $\varrho'$ of the same $E$ relative to $(\psi')^{\flat}$ such that $(E,\varrho')$ represents $(\psi',P')$; moreover the norm level transports $P_n$ along $\varrho$ and $P_n'$ along $\varrho'$ satisfy $P_n'=\chi(\tilde\theta(\gamma))\cdot P_n$; and for every prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ whose subgroup is stable under $e_\gamma$ (the Lean binder here reuses the name of the fraction field), and all extra level-$\ell$ structures $C,C'$ on $E$ which are compatible with $\varrho$, respectively $\varrho'$, in the displayed sense, the subgroups defined by $C$ and by $C'$ coincide: a point of $E$ factors through $C$ if and only if it factors through $C'$.
--
--   14.
--
--   For $(E,\varrho)$ representing $(\psi,P)$ over Noetherian connected $B$, every further curve $E'$ with a rigidification $\varrho'$ relative to $\psi^{\flat}$, every unit $h$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ and every $c\in\mathbb Z$ such that the action of $r^{c}g_0\iota_0(h)g_0^{-1}$ carries $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ to $\Xi(E',\varrho')$, and every $(\psi'',P'')$ obtained from $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $\iota_0(h)$, there is a rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E'$ relative to $(\psi'')^{\flat}$ such that $(E',\varrho'')$ represents $(\psi'',P'')$ and such that, for every prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $B$, the extra level-$\ell$ structures on $E'$ compatible with $\varrho'$ and with $\varrho''$ relative to a given extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ define the same subgroup.
--
--   15.
--
--   ($\pi$-translation) For $(E,\varrho)$ representing $(\psi,P)$, every $E'$ with a rigidification relative to some $\psi_1$, every $c\in\mathbb Z$ and every point $y$ which is a $\pi$-translate of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ and is carried to $\Xi(E',\varrho')$ by the action of $r^{c}$, there is a rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E'$ relative to $(Fr$-twist by $1$ of $\psi)^{\flat}$ such that $(E',\varrho'')$ represents $(Fr\text{-twist of }\psi,\,P)$.
--
--   16.
--
--   (Isomorphisms over a geometric point, stated over one leg) For an algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, a single $\psi$, Deligne data $P,P'$ over $k$, and pairs $(E,\varrho)$, $(E',\varrho')$ both relative to $\psi^{\flat}$ representing $(\psi,P)$ and $(\psi,P')$ respectively, every isomorphism $i:E\cong E'$ compatible with group law, $\Lambda$-action and level structure arises from some $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$: the twisted action of $\iota_0(\gamma)$ carries $(\psi,P)$ to $(\psi,P')$; the norm level transports satisfy $i_*\bigl(\chi(\tilde\theta(\gamma))\cdot P_n\bigr)=P_n'$; and for every prime $\ell\neq r$ invertible in $k$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ and all extra level-$\ell$ structures $C$ on $E$, $C'$ on $E'$ compatible with $\varrho$, respectively $\varrho'$, the statement that $i$ matches $C$ with $C'$ is equivalent to the stability of the chosen level structure on $A_0$ under $e_\gamma$.
--
--   This is the construction step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation for fake elliptic curves: from a rigidified comparison between the deformation theory of special formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules and the formal upper half-plane it produces a $\tilde\Gamma$-equivariant family of points of the fine moduli scheme $M$ over Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent, together with the level-structure, Hecke and Atkin–Lehner compatibilities needed later. This edition carries the extra hypothesis that $2$ is invertible in $\mathcal O$, and its clause on isomorphisms over a geometric point is stated over a single Frobenius leg; it is used by the companion statement without the Noetherian restriction on the parameter ring.
